```c
if ((mode->hdisplay < 1) || (mode->htotal < 1))
if ((mode->hdisplay > 0x7ff) || (mode->htotal > 0xfff))
```
Reason:
These statements check for the validity of horizontal display parameters but do not account for the pixel clock rate, which is crucial for supporting high resolutions like 1080p60. As a result, unsupported display modes may not be filtered out, leading to potential display failures.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
rounded_rate = clk_round_rate(tcon->dclk, rate);
if (rounded_rate < rate)
	return MODE_CLOCK_LOW;
if (rounded_rate > rate)
	return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
```
Reason:
These statements validate the pixel clock rate against the required rate for the display mode. By checking if the rounded clock rate is sufficient, the code ensures that only supported display modes are accepted, thus preventing display failures for high resolutions.

